\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1316348 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
2. The secret behind the happiness
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 
\par }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 HYPERLINK "https://easy-peasy.ai/ai-image-generator/images/grand-fantasy-city-crystal-tower-cathedral-urban-landscape"}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 {\*\datafield 1d}}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs27\ul\cf19\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 easy-peasy.ai}}}\sectd \ltrsect
\linex0\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Elarion's peace is maintained by a device known as the Stillheart.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Centuries ago, Elyndra suffered a devastating civil war. Generations grew up surrounded by vengeance, grief, and violence. The people were exhausted. They didn't want another king, another army, or another promise that things would get better.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 They wanted the pain to stop.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
A brilliant scholar named Aurelia Voss developed a way to regulate the emotions that drove people toward violence. Her original invention was modest: it could help people manage traumatic memories, control violent impulses, and recover from grief.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 It worked.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 At first, the Stillheart was voluntary. Soldiers used it to cope with what they had witnessed. Families used it to overcome devastating losses. Communities that had hated one another began to reconcile.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Then the government discovered something.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 People who had experienced less grief were easier to govern. People who experienced less anger were less likely to protest. People whose painful memories could be softened were less likely to seek revenge.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The system expanded.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Eventually, the Stillheart became mandatory for all citizens. Now it does more than regulate emotions. It identifies feelings considered socially disruptive and suppresses them before they can grow.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Grief. Rage. Envy. Despair.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 And, increasingly, doubt.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The citizens aren't mindless puppets. They still make choices, fall in love, pursue careers, and enjoy their lives. But their emotional range has been carefully narrowed, and their memories can be altered when they become inconvenient.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Elyndra hasn't eliminated suffering. It has eliminated the ability to respond to suffering freely.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 And the most disturbing part?
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Most citizens genuinely believe they are better off this way.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 3. The central characters
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The reluctant skeptic
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The Heart reborn
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji arrives in Elyndra hoping to find a world worth saving. Instead, he encounters people who appear happy but don't seem to understand what happiness has cost them.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 After Veyra, his patience for people who excuse harm is thinner. He doesn't hate humanity, but he's beginning to wonder why people keep building systems that hurt others\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
and then insisting those systems are necessary.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 His irritation should surface in short remarks, reluctant silences, and moments when he has to catch himself \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
before speaking harshly. He still helps people, even when he's frustrated with them.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Neris Vale \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The one who remembers
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Potential new Anchor / party member
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Neris works as a junior archivist in Elarion. Her job is to maintain public records, but she has discovered inconsistencies: people listed as married to strangers, missing years in personal histories, and official records describing events that nobody rem
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 embers.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She is one of the rare people whose mind resists the Stillheart's effects. She can feel grief and anger in full, and she refuses to let the government call those emotions defects.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Her flaw is the o\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 pposite of Elyndra's: she has become so afraid of forgetting the truth that she struggles to let go of anything painful.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Her belief: Pain is part of being alive. Removing it means removing part of yourself.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Aurelia Voss \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The architect of peace
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Founder of the Stillheart system
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Aurelia is not a cackling villain. She remembers the civil war. She remembers children dying because their parents could not forgive each other. She has watched grief turn into revenge and revenge turn into another generation of funerals.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She genuinely believes she saved Elyndra.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 When confronted with the system's abuses, she doesn't deny them. She argues that the alternative is worse\hich\f31506 \emdash \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
and that people who have never lived through the war have no right to demand that others endure it again.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Her belief: Freedom is meaningless if people use it to destroy one another.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Tavian \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The happy citizen
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 A human cost, not a secret villain
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Tavian is a close friend of Neris and a genuinely decent person. He volunteers at a public garden, cares for elderly neighbors, and believes the Stillheart gave him his life back after a terrible childhood.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He knows the system suppresses pain. He simply doesn't believe that makes it wrong.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 When Neris discovers that Tavian's sister was taken into a memory-correction program after protesting the government, Tavian insists his sister must have needed help.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 His defense is sincere. That's what makes it hurt.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 His belief: If a system lets people live peacefully, perhaps the price is worth paying.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 4. The story, chapter by chapter
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Chapter I \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  A World That Smiles
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji and the party arrive through the Eldergate portal in a secluded garden outside Elarion.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The first thing they notice is how quiet it is.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 A child drops a glass ornament. It shatters. The child's parent kneels, smiles, and tells them it's all right. The child smiles back immediately, without a trace of distress.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 After the hardship of Veyra, the city feels like a miracle.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The party is welcomed by city attendants, who offer food, lodging, and medical treatment. No one demands payment. No one seems afraid of strangers.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Then Neris approaches them privately. She has noticed the unfamiliar mark on Kenji's hand, and she ha\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 s a question she cannot ask anyone else.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Do you remember everything that makes you unhappy?"
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji thinks she's joking.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She tells him that the city's central tower can alter memories\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 and that someone has been erasing records of people who question it.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She asks for help finding her missing mentor, an archivist who discovered something beneath the tower.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji agrees. Not because he's convinced the city is evil, but because someone is missing and no one else seems concerned.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The first hint of irritation: When a city official assures Kenji that all missing citizens are receiving appropriate care, he asks whether anyone actually bothered to ask those citizens what they wanted.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The official smiles.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Of course. Their preferences are carefully considered."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji looks at Neris.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "That's not what I asked."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 It's a small moment. He doesn't start a fight. But he's beginning to recognize the language people use to avoid answering for themselves.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Chapter II \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The Happiness Protocol
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Neris leads the party into the lower districts, where citizens who have resisted memory correction are quietly relocated.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Here, the perfection of Elarion begins to fracture.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 A woman recognizes Kenji's party and begs them to help her find her son. Before she can explain, an attendant arrives with a calming device. The woman sees it and immediately apologizes for causing a disturbance.

\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She forgets why she was upset.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Later, Kenji finds her sitting alone, smiling at nothing.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Neris explains that the woman has been searching for her son for months. Her memories of him are repeatedly suppressed because her grief has become classified as destabilizing.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji is furious.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 But the woman, when approached, insists that she is fine. She thanks the authorities for helping her feel better.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji struggles with that. He wants to rescue her, but he cannot simply decide that she must suffer because he believes suffering is necessary.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Neris tells him the woman's \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 ability to choose has been compromised.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 This becomes the moral center of the chapter: does respecting someone's wishes mean accepting them when the system has altered the person making the choice?
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The party discovers that Neris's mentor is alive beneath the central tower, imprisoned in an archival facility where memories are edited and stored.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 And they find evidence that the Stillheart is no longer merely suppressing dangerous emotions. It is being used to erase political dissent.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Chapter III \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The People \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Who Chose This
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The party exposes the program to a group of citizens who have begun to resist.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji expects them to be horrified.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Instead, they argue.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Some citizens want the system dismantled immediately. Others fear that without it, old rivalries will return. One woman says her husband was violent before the Stillheart and that she is alive because the system changed him. A former soldier says the devi
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 ce is the only reason he can sleep without reliving the war.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Their fear is real. Their relief is real.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 So \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 is the injustice.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Aurelia appears before the party and offers to show Kenji the city's historical records. She doesn't threaten him. She walks him through the ruins of the old civil war and the memorials to its dead.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She explains that the Stillheart began as a voluntary treatment, created by people who could not bear to lose another generation to violence.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Then she asks him a question:
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "How many people must suffer so that you can preserve the right to suffer?"
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 It's the first time Kenji has no immediate \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 answer.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 After all he's seen, he cannot dismiss the fear behind her question. But he also can't accept a world where people are made peaceful by having their choices taken away.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Aurelia offers him a compromise: help her repair the Stillheart, and she will preserve the city's peace while ending the worst abuses.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji is tempted. The offer is reasonable on the surface. It would save lives without destroying everything the people rely on.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 But Neris discovers that the system's instability is not an accident. \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Its designers have been expanding its control because it has become dependent on a constant supply of emotional energy and memory patterns.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Repairing it without changing its purpose would only prolong the cycle.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Chapter IV \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Beneath the Stillheart
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 
\par }{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
HYPERLINK "https://www.thepopverse.com/gaming-final-fantasy-xvi-16-magic-the-gathering-wizards-of-the-coast-employees-release-date-wild-weekend"}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 {\*\datafield 11}}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cs27\ul\cf19\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 thepopverse.com}}}\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Beneath the tower, the party discovers the Stillheart's original core. I\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
t was built to help people process pain, not erase it. Over generations, layers of new machinery have transformed it into a device that extracts and suppresses emotional responses.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The core is now destabilizing. It is drawing more and more from the citizens to maintain the appearance of perfect peace.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The Mind's influence is present here\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 but su\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
btle. Old inscriptions in the machine's deepest chamber describe a philosophy that treats suffering as a problem to be removed rather than an experience to be understood. Someone has been feeding Aurelia fragments of ancient knowledge, nudging her toward 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 a more absolute solution.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The Mind didn't create Aurelia's grief or force the city to adopt the Stillheart. It recognized her fear and helped her turn a limited invention into an answer for everything.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The final confrontation is with Aurelia and the Stillheart's protective system.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Aurelia fights because she believes the party will unleash the same chaos that once devastated Elyndra. She is not trying to rule the world for power. She is trying to stop history from repeating itself.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 When the machine begins to fail, the party has to choose how to dismantle it. Simply destroying the core would release the suppressed emotions all at once, risking panic and violence throughout the city.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Kenji's mark responds to the original mechanism beneath the accumulated machinery. Just as he restored balance to Veyra's Emberheart, he discovers a way to reconnect the Stillheart to its original purpose: helping people face their emotions, rather than s
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 tripping them away.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 But the process cannot make the consequences disappear.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Citizens will have to confront grief they barely remember. Families will learn what was done to them. Some people will be angry. Some will reject the truth. Some will even \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
beg for the old system back.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The city will not be healed overnight.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Aurelia survives, forced to face a future she can no longer control.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 And Neris must learn that remembering everything is not the same as knowing how to live with it.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Chapter V \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  The First Honest Tears
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 In the aftermath, Kenji sees Tavian standing beside his sister, who has finally been released from the memory-correction program.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 She remembers what happened to her. She is angry with him for defending the system, and he cannot find the words \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 to answer her.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 For the first time in years, Tavian cries.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He doesn't look relieved. He doesn't look happy.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He looks human.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji watches them from a distance. Neris joins him and asks if he thinks they did the right thing.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Kenji takes a while to answer.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "I think we gave them the choice."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Neris asks if that is enough.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He looks across the city. Some citizens are embracing. Others are arguing in the streets. An old man sits beside a memorial and weeps for a wife he can finally remember.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "I don't know," Kenji \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 admits. "But at least this time, it's their choice to make."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The portal reactivates. As the party prepares to leave, Kenji notices a symbol etched into the Stillheart's oldest foundation\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 a mark resembling the one on his hand.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Someone had been here long before he arrived.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Someone knew what this world might become.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 And someone wanted him to see it.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 5. Kenji's character arc: irritation, not hatred
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 I want to keep this restrained. Kenji should not suddenly become a brooding anti-human protagonist. The change is \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
more interesting if it shows up in little flashes that even he may not fully notice.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 EARLY KENJI \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  AFTER VEYRA
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "They were scared. I get it. But they still had a choice."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He believes people can do better when they are given the chance.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 MID-STORY \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  IN ELYNDRA
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Funny how the people making the rules never seem to be the ones paying for them."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He starts recognizing the pattern: people in power call their sacrifices necessary when someone else bears the cost.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 LATE-STORY \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  AFTER AURELIA'S OFFER
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Every time someone\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  says they're doing this for everyone's good, I start wondering who 'everyone' actually means."
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He is more suspicious, more easily frustrated, but still willing to listen. The danger is not that he stops caring; it's that he begins to expect the worst.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The important distinction is that Kenji's frustration is directed at humanity's habit of turning fear into justification. He can understand why people make terrible choices without accepting those choices as inevitable.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 That is exactly what the Mind wants to \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 exploit.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The Mind doesn't need Kenji to witness evil. He has already seen it. It needs Kenji to conclude that evil is the unavoidable result of human nature\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
and that trying to save people is an endless, pointless cycle.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Elyndra is the next step in that argument. Veyra showed Kenji people sacrificing others to survive. Elyndra shows him people surrendering their freedom to escape pain, then defending the system that took it.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 And after both worlds, Kenji might begin to wonder whether the Mind has a point.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 won't agree with it. Not yet.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 But for the first time, when the Mind eventually argues that existence only creates suffering, Kenji will have memories that make the argument harder to dismiss.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 6. What portal world #2 adds to the larger JRPG
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls3\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid1316348 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
A new Anchor: Neris joins the party as someone who believes pain and memory are essential to being human. Her personal journey challenges Kenji's growing frustration by showing him that people can be both victims of a system and defenders of it.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 A different kind of \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
victory: The party cannot simply defeat a monster and restore everything. They must give a society the chance to make difficult choices for itself.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
A more sophisticated antagonist: The Mind's influence becomes clearer without turning every tragedy into its direct creation. It exploits existing fears and gives people arguments for doing what they already want to do.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
A subtle shift in Kenji: He still chooses to help, but he becomes less patient with comforting lies and noble excuses. That can create friction with future companions who genuinely believe order, sacrifice, or obedience are necessary.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \loch\af3\dbch\af31505\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
A question that follows the party: If suffering is part of freedom, what obligations do people have to one another? And when does protecting someone become controlling them?
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1316348 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348\charrsid1316348 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
My favorite part of this world is that the Mind's argument should feel a little more convincing to the player, too. Aurelia has real reasons for what she did. Some citizens genuinely benefited from the system. Dismantling it causes pain. The party makes t
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 he right choice not because the alternative has no merit, but because a life without meaningful choice is not a life the party has the right to impose.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 That gives Kenji a much more compelling journey than simply learning that people can be cruel. He already knows that.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 He's learning how easy it is for people\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 including good people\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 to convince themselves that cruelty is kindness.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1316348 
